{"step_index":110,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-23T00:39:02Z","thinking":"The `nCurrentSelection` variable directly dictates the touchpad mode setting. Previously, different button clicks were mapped to values. `Grid_MouseLeftButtonUp_1`, `Grid_MouseLeftButtonUp_2`, and `Grid_MouseLeftButtonUp_3` correspond to 0, 1, and 2, respectively. The touchpad mode therefore can be 0 (on), 1 (off), or 2 (auto).\n\n\nInitially, the touchpad is disabled in the registry and the ACPI controller indicates an \"auto/off when mouse present\" state (value 2). Calling the `Set_TouchPadMode(0)` function sets the ACPI method to 0, which enables the touchpad at the hardware level. This corresponds to writing \"0\" to the registry key, and the state change event is fired.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"powershell -NoProfile -Command \"`$asm = [System.Reflection.Assembly]::LoadFrom('C:\\Program Files (x86)\\LG Software\\LG OSD\\HotkeyManager.exe'); foreach(`$t in `$asm.GetTypes()){ foreach(`$m in `$t.GetMethods([Reflection.BindingFlags]'Public,NonPublic,Instance,Static')){ if (`$m.Name -match 'Touch|F5') { Write-Host (`$t.FullName + '::' + `$m.Name) } } }\"","Cwd":"c:\\Users\\lg\\fix","WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolAction":"Searching HotkeyManager for Touchpad handlers","toolSummary":"Search HotkeyManager"}}]}
